# Cross-repo siblings cloned by setup-dev-env at workspace-lock-pinned
# revisions (see codetracer-specs/Testing/Cross-Repo-CI-Integration.md).

# The package catalog `repro.nim`'s `uses: "sqlite3"` resolves from. sqlite3
# is no longer bundled with reprobuild's stdlib; reprobuild looks it up in a
# `reprobuild-packages` checkout beside this one, and a recipe that uses a moved
# package with no catalog reachable does not compile. Only the reprobuild-flavor
# job compiles `repro.nim`; the nix jobs never do (their `sqlite3` tool is
# `pkgs.sqlite` in the dev shell).
#
# Pinned to an exact revision (reprobuild-packages 56ffd67, the catalog of
# reprobuild 33be1e9964, published on its `agents` branch; it declares the
# version of sqlite3's Windows archives, which `uses: "sqlite3 >=3"` needs)
# rather than `=dev`, which clone-siblings warns makes the build not
# reproducible. The
# catalog is also locked by the flake input used by the owning Nix shell.
# Keep this non-Nix CI pin aligned with that source constructor.
reprobuild-packages=92100803eb827ff21d0cc48b7474fb0a65057cbd

# RunQuota's source-library siblings, cloned at the revisions repro.lock
# records for them (`deps`). They are bare names on purpose: the repro engine
# refuses a checkout whose HEAD differs from the revision the consumer lock
# expects ("cross-repo producer ... source revision mismatch"), so any revision
# written here can only go stale when the lock moves. The earlier overrides
# (nim-shm-lease 22e3100c, nim-shm-queue 84fd76b1) existed only to match the
# lock of 2026-11-04; the lock now pins descendants of both.
nim-shm-lease
# Transitive source dependency of shm_lease/obsring.
nim-shm-queue
